From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm forward: the prompt pieces' ranges and events beside the pieced exchanges

zig/src/families/glm/cuda_forward.zig is 600 lines at v1.2.7, the lean rule's limit, and the index, one-pass,
chunked-KDA and MLA levers later in this series add lines to it. row_step, max_pieces, ranges() and the Pieces
struct move, unchanged, to cuda_forward_pieces.zig, which already holds the pieced exchanges that use them;
cuda_forward.zig re-exports max_pieces, ranges and Pieces, so every caller (cuda_engine, cuda_prompt_pair,
cuda_forward_pair) reads them as before. No behaviour changes.

Re-seated on v1.2.7 (93a2e93ecebff8aa52b88e58c5dd222516e69c5f, from pin 9c9bf542) by the 2026-11-12 re-seat:
- cuda_forward.zig 600 -> 542 lines; the fold's sparse-onepass moved ranges() alone into cuda_forward_pair.zig for the same rule, which this move replaces.

